    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d848">

                <pb facs="0914" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg794"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Russian
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to my informal
                    note of the 2d ultimo, I beg to inform you that I am advised by the Acting
                    Secretary of the Navy that the officers of the interned Russian war vessels at
                    Manila whose names are given below have signed the parole not to further engage
                    in the present war with Japan and have been authorized to leave the immediate
                    vicinity of Manila and to return to Russia: Lieut. D. de Daehn, I. R. Navy;
                    Lieut. A. Losseff, I. R. Navy; Sublieut. M. Bertenson, I. R. Navy; Sublieut. V.
                    Iakovleff, I. R. Navy.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
